01:29.660 --> 01:33.740
The Most Outstanding Players of the tournament will now be announced.

01:33.740 --> 01:38.830
These 24 players were chosen to be part of the Japanese Junior Youth team.

01:38.830 --> 01:40.630
Without further ado, here are the players:

01:40.630 --> 01:45.780
Goalkeepers: Wakashimazu-kun, Morisaki-kun, and Kato-kun.

01:45.780 --> 01:51.540
Defenders: Ishizaki-kun, Takasugi-kun, Jito-kun, and Soda-kun.

01:51.540 --> 02:01.180
Midfielders: Ohzara-kun, Izawa-kun, Matsuyama-kun, Sawada-kun, Koike-kun, Ishida-kun, and Mori-kun.

02:01.180 --> 02:06.980
Forwards: Hyuga-kun, Sorimachi-kun, Sano-kun, Oda-kun...{}{}{TLC: ",Ooda-kun..."}

02:05.900 --> 02:08.070
My predictions were correct.

02:08.680 --> 02:12.520
With these players, this team will make a name for itself in the world.

02:13.220 --> 02:15.660
They truly are the best members.

02:17.660 --> 02:22.840
<b>Go for it! Japanese Junior Youth Team!</b>

02:17.770 --> 02:22.840
<b>Go for it! Japanese Junior Youth Team!</b>

02:33.580 --> 02:35.500
We're finally going out in the world.

02:35.500 --> 02:41.630
Yeah, but I still can't believe it. Me? On the Japanese National team?

02:41.630 --> 02:44.440
And what's more, we might even get to go to France!

02:44.440 --> 02:46.500
It feels like my heart's gonna explode!

02:46.960 --> 02:49.490
Hey! Tsubasa! Ishizaki!

02:50.020 --> 02:51.340
Guys!

02:51.710 --> 02:52.350
Yo!

02:52.350 --> 02:54.980
How's your shoulder Tsubasa?

02:54.980 --> 02:56.730
It's already much better.

02:56.730 --> 03:00.190
But the doctor isn't letting me practice much.

03:00.190 --> 03:03.200
It's because you put too much into it right away.

03:06.090 --> 03:09.660
But that's also what makes you so good Tsubasa.

03:17.010 --> 03:21.390
Everyone, and by that I mean you, the Japanese Junior Youth team.

03:21.390 --> 03:24.300
We will now begin the presentation on our joint training camp.

03:31.180 --> 03:32.700
Misugi-kun?

03:35.460 --> 03:38.620
Misugi-kun's... a coach?

03:40.200 --> 03:42.930
As you all know,

03:42.930 --> 03:47.890
the Junior Youth Championship will be held in France this year.

03:48.480 --> 03:51.640
There will be 12 countries participating in this championship,

03:51.640 --> 03:56.960
where teams featuring the most promising future stars

03:56.960 --> 03:59.580
under the age of 15 will battle for first place.

04:00.380 --> 04:02.930
As representatives of Japan...

04:02.930 --> 04:05.810
I offer encouragement and wish you nothing but the best.

04:05.820 --> 04:09.420
Now, we present you the coaching staff.

04:09.420 --> 04:11.440
First, Coach Mikami.

04:11.440 --> 04:16.780
He was a long time member of the national team as a goal keeper,

04:16.780 --> 04:19.690
and has trained numerous teams.

04:19.690 --> 04:24.270
He's currently training the Grunwald squad, of which Wakabayashi-kun is a member.

04:25.400 --> 04:28.370
To his right is Coach Kato Mitsugi.

04:29.340 --> 04:34.690
Coach Kato is a former forward on the national team, and also has the title of "Top Goal Scorer" in the J-league.

04:35.390 --> 04:37.780
Finally, Coach Misugi Jun.

04:38.210 --> 04:41.780
As you probably know, he's currently the 
captain of Musashi Middle School's team.

04:43.150 --> 04:48.130
However he's not here for the tournament as a player, but as a coach.  {}{}{TLC: to clear up any confusions, I'd put it as "However he's not here for the tournament as a player, but as a coach."}

04:48.780 --> 04:51.780
We will be utilizing his keen observation skills and level-headed approach for the game.

04:51.780 --> 04:53.560
And seeing as he's the same age as you,

04:53.560 --> 04:57.820
he'll be able to train you the best.

04:58.280 --> 05:03.340
I know it's rather sudden, but starting tomorrow, you'll be training in Fukushima.

05:03.840 --> 05:09.820
After some intensive training, we will decide just who is going to Europe for the championship.

05:10.100 --> 05:15.540
Before the championship in France, there will be a training session in Germany.

05:19.980 --> 05:23.290
I'm taking the defender spot, Ishizaki.

05:23.650 --> 05:26.300
What the heck are you talking about? I'm not gonna lose to you!

05:27.840 --> 05:29.310
See you after tomorrow.

05:29.310 --> 05:31.060
Yeah. See ya.

05:34.600 --> 05:35.740
Misugi-kun.

05:35.740 --> 05:38.020
Misugi! I was so surprised earlier!

05:39.360 --> 05:45.290
It's a pity I wasn't chosen as a player, but I'll do my best as a coach this time.

05:45.290 --> 05:45.780
Let's do our best!

05:45.780 --> 05:49.540
With your strategy and judgement, it'll be a cinch.

05:49.540 --> 05:54.240
If the reason I wasn't chosen is because of my heart problems,

05:54.240 --> 05:57.520
it means I'm not strong enough.

05:58.370 --> 06:03.130
But it doesn't mean I'm giving up on my wish to be a part of the Japanese National team.

06:04.510 --> 06:06.420
I have a dream.

06:06.420 --> 06:07.690
A dream?

06:07.690 --> 06:08.330
Yeah.

06:08.330 --> 06:14.940
Yeah. A dream where I'm selected to the national team, and I'm able to play with you guys in the International Cup.

06:14.940 --> 06:17.300
The International Cup?

06:17.300 --> 06:22.910
By "International Cup" do you mean the International Cup that decides the world champs? {}{}{TLC: By "International Cup" do you mean the International Cup that decides the world champs?}

06:22.910 --> 06:23.930
Yeah.

06:24.200 --> 06:27.340
Eh? But don't you think that's a bit too much?

06:27.780 --> 06:31.620
I don't think it's an unattainable dream.

06:31.620 --> 06:34.780
Actually, I know we'll be able to do it. {}{}{TLC: have something for that "iya" at the beginning like "actually" or "no"}

06:39.680 --> 06:40.470
Yeah.

06:41.870 --> 06:44.260
Let's make that dream come true, Misugi-kun.

06:44.900 --> 06:48.780
We'll make that dream come true together!

06:49.060 --> 06:49.930
Yes.

06:51.320 --> 06:53.040
Alright, let's do it!

06:53.040 --> 06:55.450
The International Cup, eh? Alright!

06:55.450 --> 06:57.700
It's like something big just happened! {Was: Let's aim for something incredible!}

06:57.700 --> 06:59.910
Dreams have to be grand.

06:59.910 --> 07:02.700
First, we have the championship in France. Let's do our best!

07:02.700 --> 07:03.500
Yeah.

07:03.500 --> 07:04.890
Let's do it! {Was: We'll do everything in order to succeed!}

07:03.820 --> 07:04.890
Ohzara.

07:04.890 --> 07:06.420
Ohzara! Come over here for a moment.

07:07.270 --> 07:08.400
Yes, sir!

07:08.400 --> 07:10.790
We'll go on ahead then.

07:13.500 --> 07:16.250
This is about the training camp coming up.

07:16.640 --> 07:17.450
Yes?

07:18.340 --> 07:21.180
You don't need to take part.

07:22.360 --> 07:24.620
Your first priority is to heal your shoulder.

07:25.060 --> 07:29.100
That's the most important thing you need to do right now, Ohzara.

07:30.210 --> 07:32.950
Yes, I understand.

07:46.460 --> 07:48.570
In the practice game against the high-school team... {}{}{TLC: In the practice game against the high-school team}

07:49.230 --> 07:53.080
I wonder what kind of challenge they will be? {}{}{TLC: I wonder what kind of challenge they will be?}

07:53.820 --> 07:54.860
Here they are!

07:56.330 --> 08:00.740
The most reputed team in high-school soccer: Mihara Central High School. {}{}{TLC: The most reputed team in high-school soccer: Mihara Central High School}

08:04.940 --> 08:07.530
Nankatsu Hospital

08:07.540 --> 08:09.740
<b>Consulation Room Surgical Section</b>

08:13.630 --> 08:15.020
Do you feel pain here?

08:16.600 --> 08:17.540
A bit.

08:18.070 --> 08:22.780
You're doing much better, but you still can't force yourself too much.

08:23.650 --> 08:26.220
Um, what about soccer?

08:27.140 --> 08:29.220
You'll still have to wait.

08:36.320 --> 08:39.820
A "2 - 1" win in their first game against a high school team. Not bad.

08:40.850 --> 08:45.700
Misugi-kun, who do you see starting at the different positions?

08:45.700 --> 08:51.440
Well, first I think we have to create a solid line in the center.

08:51.440 --> 08:53.810
The goal keeper should be Wakashimazu.

08:53.810 --> 08:55.380
Libero: Matsuyama.

08:55.380 --> 08:57.120
Midfielder: Ohzara.

08:57.120 --> 08:58.500
Forward: Hyuga.

08:58.780 --> 09:02.900
Defenders: Takasugi, Jito, and Soda.

09:03.500 --> 09:07.440
Midfielders are: Sano and the younger Tachibana. {}{}{TLC: Midfielders are: Sano and the younger Tachibana.}

09:07.440 --> 09:10.900
The other forwards: Nitta, and the older Tachibana brother.

09:12.090 --> 09:13.420
What do you think?

09:13.420 --> 09:15.470
4-3-3, huh?

09:15.470 --> 09:17.890
That's almost exactly what I was thinking,

09:17.890 --> 09:21.000
still, we can put Matsuyama on as a defender? {}{}{TLC: still, we can put Matsuyama on as a defender?}

09:21.630 --> 09:25.230
Yes, he's good at decision making and has a good field of vision. {}{}{TLC: Yes, he's a good decision-maker and can see all around him.}

09:25.230 --> 09:29.480
Plus he's a physical player, so I think he'll make a good defender.

09:29.480 --> 09:34.980
However, this strategy depends entirely on Tsubasa-kun playing.

09:34.980 --> 09:35.820
Yeah, that's true.

09:36.210 --> 09:41.860
Um, Coach... Do you think this will probably be too hard on Tsubasa-kun?

09:42.800 --> 09:44.990
If his shoulder isn't completely healed,

09:44.990 --> 09:47.340
I will think of a line-up without him. {}{}{TLC: I will think of a line-up without him.}

09:57.580 --> 09:59.140
Damn it.

09:59.140 --> 10:02.240
While everbody's working hard and aiming for the world,

10:02.240 --> 10:03.380
I...

10:06.530 --> 10:09.590
The first game in Europe is against Grunwald.

10:11.170 --> 10:16.460
There are numerous players all over the world that even you couldn't match up to.

10:34.500 --> 10:38.920
"As a soccer player, you have to accept injuries."

10:39.670 --> 10:44.880
"Waiting for an injury to heal is the shortest path on a long journey."

10:46.150 --> 10:47.420
Roberto...

10:50.820 --> 10:54.220
How stupid of me. What am I being impatient for?

10:57.320 --> 11:00.240
All right. First, I'll let this shoulder heal,

11:00.240 --> 11:01.860
and after that, I'll challenge the world!

11:15.250 --> 11:16.370
Schneider.

11:16.370 --> 11:17.890
Wakabayashi.

11:17.890 --> 11:21.340
My transfer to Rotburg is now official.

11:21.700 --> 11:23.580
Oh yeah? Good for you!

11:24.830 --> 11:27.820
What do you say? One last challenge, Wakabayashi?

11:28.200 --> 11:30.360
All right, let's do it! Come on!

11:33.540 --> 11:35.870
I'll shoot from outside the penalty area.

11:36.480 --> 11:37.630
And without further ado,

11:37.630 --> 11:38.340
here I go!

11:38.340 --> 11:39.380
Bring it!

11:41.460 --> 11:44.860
Take this! Fire Shot!

11:54.100 --> 11:56.240
I-It's in.

11:56.240 --> 11:58.100
Schneider won.

11:58.100 --> 12:01.740
With this, we're 50/50.

12:01.740 --> 12:05.540
Your shot's gotten even better.

12:05.540 --> 12:10.020
So have you. One of these days you'll be a player in the Bundesliga. {Was: in the first division of German leagues. Is this correct?}{yeah}

12:10.840 --> 12:14.250
When that day comes, we'll decide who's the winner, Wakabayashi.

12:14.250 --> 12:17.500
Yeah, I'll be sure to take the same path as you in the future.

12:17.500 --> 12:24.020
I'll challenge you as the regular goalkeeper for Grunwald, Schneider.{}{}{TLC: switch "entitled" with "regular"}

12:29.020 --> 12:31.260
Are you leaving for Rotburg right away?

12:31.990 --> 12:38.260
No, I still have one game left with Grunwald.

12:38.740 --> 12:43.660
The game against the Japanese Junior Youth team that's coming to Europe, eh?

12:43.660 --> 12:44.340
Yeah.

12:44.340 --> 12:47.260
I'm greatly anticipating seeing what kind of player that,

12:47.260 --> 12:50.030
Ohzara Tsubasa you've always talked about is.

12:51.320 --> 12:53.410
I'm looking forward to it too.

13:07.120 --> 13:09.210
Tsubasa, breakfast's ready!

13:09.700 --> 13:11.020
Okay!

13:13.080 --> 13:16.620
Ishizaki-kun and the team are in the newspaper.

13:17.230 --> 13:18.610
They really are!

13:18.610 --> 13:24.380
"Japanese Junior Youth team member Hyuga Kojiro's team, the Tiger Shots, won two games

13:24.380 --> 13:29.770
against Mihara and Teiwa High Schools, with scores of 2 - 1 and 2 - 0."

13:29.770 --> 13:35.780
"They are next scheduled to play the number one high school in the country, Toho Academy." {}{}{TLC: They are next scheduled to play the number one high school in the country, Toho Academy.}

13:36.610 --> 13:38.940
So the next game's against Toho Academy.

13:39.780 --> 13:41.940
They're all doing their best.

13:44.180 --> 13:45.060
Itadakimasu!

13:46.170 --> 13:49.380
Tsubasa, what about giving them a visit?

13:51.450 --> 13:52.940
Oh, you can't do that?

13:53.560 --> 13:55.940
No, there shouldn't be any reason not to, but...

13:56.370 --> 13:58.260
Why not then?

13:58.260 --> 14:01.840
You must be bored training alone every day.

14:01.840 --> 14:02.900
You should go!

14:03.920 --> 14:04.870
Yeah.

14:05.900 --> 14:09.470
Coach Mikami, to beat high school teams is rather incredible, isn't it?

14:09.470 --> 14:12.510
Is winning some games in France within the realm of possibility?

14:12.510 --> 14:16.800
We can finally talk about a real team that can rival the whole world, can't we?

14:17.450 --> 14:21.140
It's our job to train them to that level.

14:21.640 --> 14:24.770
Are you aiming for the International Cup in the future?

14:24.770 --> 14:26.260
The thought has crossed my mind. {Was: Of course I've given that some thought.}

14:37.150 --> 14:38.500
Tsubasa!

14:38.860 --> 14:40.160
Hey, guys!

14:42.240 --> 14:43.710
How's your shoulder?

14:43.710 --> 14:46.140
I've just started to do a bit of stretching.

14:46.140 --> 14:46.700
I see.

14:46.700 --> 14:50.730
Hurry up and get better, or your position will be taken.

14:51.360 --> 14:54.350
Will you be ready by the time we go to Europe?

14:54.350 --> 14:56.220
Of course he will! Right, Tsubasa?

14:56.220 --> 14:58.700
We're going to France with our best players.

14:58.940 --> 14:59.810
Right.

15:02.210 --> 15:03.460
Coach!

15:03.460 --> 15:06.100
Toho Academy's team is here.

15:06.750 --> 15:07.530
Here they are.

15:07.530 --> 15:10.740
The National Intramural Champion, Toho Academy's high school team.

15:12.410 --> 15:15.940
I'm interested in seeing how far the Junior Youth team can go.

15:28.180 --> 15:29.260
Damn it!

15:31.300 --> 15:35.300
We should have known Toho wasn't gonna let us run roughshod all over them!

15:36.390 --> 15:37.620
Tsubasa-kun,

15:37.620 --> 15:44.300
if you were in the midfield, this game would be completely different, don't you think?

15:45.440 --> 15:48.300
Same goes for you, Misugi-kun.

15:49.040 --> 15:52.670
If you were on the pitch, it wouldn't be like this.

15:54.340 --> 15:56.540
I want to go out there... on the pitch.

15:58.520 --> 15:59.580
Yeah...

16:01.580 --> 16:02.420
All right!

16:10.420 --> 16:12.420
Toho High School

16:10.420 --> 16:12.420
Junior Youth National Team

16:27.540 --> 16:29.540
Toho High School

16:27.540 --> 16:29.540
Junior Youth National Team

16:30.000 --> 16:32.370
They're playing great!

16:32.370 --> 16:33.020
They do.

16:33.940 --> 16:35.360
Hey, guys!

16:35.360 --> 16:38.700
There's only one minute left. Keep going until the end!

16:38.700 --> 16:39.700
Tsubasa!

16:39.700 --> 16:40.420
Tsubasa...

16:39.700 --> 16:40.980
Tsubasa.

16:41.370 --> 16:42.560
Pass me the ball!

16:42.560 --> 16:43.020
Yeah!

16:49.550 --> 16:50.980
This is incredible!

16:50.980 --> 16:51.700
They can do it!

16:51.990 --> 16:52.580
Soda!

16:52.580 --> 16:53.710
Leave it to me!

16:54.820 --> 16:55.780
It's Soda's Razor Pass!

16:55.780 --> 16:57.950
The fact that you're the number one high school team

16:57.950 --> 16:59.780
doesn't matter!

16:59.780 --> 17:03.780
I'm the striker for Japan, and I'm gonna score!

17:09.980 --> 17:12.140
This can't be happening, right?

17:12.140 --> 17:13.410
All right!

17:13.410 --> 17:14.570
We won!

17:14.570 --> 17:15.860
Three wins in a row!

17:16.430 --> 17:18.750
All right! That's the way to do it!

17:21.830 --> 17:26.900
I'm now announcing the players going to Europe.

17:31.900 --> 17:33.620
Europe Tourney Members: Hyuga Kojirou as Captain, Sugimachi Kazuki, Kisugi Teppei, 
Sano Mitsuru, Taki Hajime, Nitta Shun, Matsuyama Hikaru as Vice-captain, Tachibana
 Masao, Tachibana Kazuo, Sawada Takeshi, Izawa Mamoru, Takasugi Shingo
  Ishizaki Ryo, Jito Hiroshi, Soda Makoto, Wakabayashi Genzo, Morisaki Yuzo. {QC: Should I remove this?}

17:33.620 --> 17:37.640
Europe Tourney Members: Hyuga Kojirou as Captain, Sugimachi Kazuki, Kisugi Teppei, Sano Mitsuru, Taki Hajime, Nitta Shun, Matsuyama Hikaru as Vice-captain, Tachibana Masao, Tachibana Kazuo, Sawada Takeshi, Izawa Mamoru, Takasugi Shingo  Ishizaki Ryo, Jito Hiroshi, Soda Makoto, Wakabayashi Genzo, Morisaki Yuzo. {QC: Should I remove this?}

17:37.650 --> 17:40.420
I'm in! My name's there!

17:40.420 --> 17:43.660
I... am... the captain of the Japanese team...

17:47.190 --> 17:48.840
Tsubasa, I'm in!

17:48.840 --> 17:51.670
I'll be going to France along with you!

17:51.670 --> 17:53.370
Congratulations, Ishizaki.

17:57.340 --> 18:00.050
Tsubasa... But why?!

18:01.020 --> 18:02.490
There's nothing we can do about it.

18:02.490 --> 18:03.540
It must be a lie, right?

18:04.040 --> 18:06.540
Why aren't we going together?!

18:10.540 --> 18:14.390
My injury's not completely healed, so it can't be helped.

18:14.390 --> 18:15.860
Tsubasa...

18:16.430 --> 18:18.220
Tsubasa-kun!

18:28.710 --> 18:30.000
Thank you very much!

18:30.000 --> 18:31.770
Hey, turn this way, please!

18:33.430 --> 18:34.760
Good luck in battle!

18:34.760 --> 18:35.330
Yes.

18:36.990 --> 18:40.410
Wow! What a big crowd!

18:41.570 --> 18:43.240
Isn't that Tsubasa?

18:43.240 --> 18:44.050
Tsubasa!

18:44.050 --> 18:45.160
It's him!

18:44.350 --> 18:45.160
Tsubasa?

18:45.600 --> 18:47.710
You came, Tsubasa!

18:50.430 --> 18:51.420
Hyuga.

18:51.420 --> 18:51.740
Yeah.

18:52.850 --> 18:55.740
There's something I wanna give you, Tsubasa.

18:59.290 --> 19:01.020
I'll be waiting, Tsubasa.

19:07.200 --> 19:08.420
It's yours.

19:13.770 --> 19:18.220
But this is a uniform for the Japanese National team, and I'm not part of it...

19:18.220 --> 19:23.000
The coach told us to choose the number we wanted,

19:23.000 --> 19:27.740
but nobody took number ten.

19:29.140 --> 19:34.720
Number ten on this Japanese Junior National team is you, Tsubasa.

19:34.720 --> 19:36.540
That's right!

19:37.020 --> 19:40.860
Everybody knows that the only proper number for Tsubasa is number ten.

19:41.810 --> 19:42.870
Yeah.

19:45.030 --> 19:46.210
Guys...

19:51.690 --> 19:53.180
Tsubasa...

19:54.280 --> 19:58.620
I want to go to Europe even more now.

19:59.850 --> 20:02.500
It is now 13:32.

20:02.500 --> 20:07.500
Boarding for flight number 451 with connecting flight in Bangkok will now begin...

20:07.500 --> 20:10.260
Okay, it's time to set off!

20:10.260 --> 20:12.240
Yeah!

20:12.240 --> 20:14.100
Let's go. See ya.

20:15.080 --> 20:19.820
Would all passengers please make their way toward the south terminal. {}{}{TLC: Yes, it's wings, as in "wings of a building". But "terminal" is more common for an airport. -Das}

20:22.580 --> 20:23.650
Ohzara.

20:24.920 --> 20:26.380
Coach Mikami.

20:26.700 --> 20:30.380
I'm gonna make sure my shoulder heals in less than two weeks.

20:31.190 --> 20:32.860
So please, put me...

20:35.820 --> 20:38.220
It's your ticket to France.

20:38.830 --> 20:41.400
The number ten for the Japanese National team

20:41.400 --> 20:43.680
can only be you, Ohzara.

20:43.680 --> 20:44.770
Coach...

20:44.770 --> 20:49.400
With its number ten, and its 
number 11 who is in France,

20:49.400 --> 20:52.220
this national team will be complete.

20:52.220 --> 20:55.860
Who's the number 11 in France?

20:55.860 --> 20:57.580
It's Misaki Taro.

20:58.600 --> 20:59.780
Misaki-kun!

21:00.930 --> 21:03.260
I'll be waiting for you in France.

21:04.200 --> 21:05.130
Yes, sir!

21:25.000 --> 21:29.700
So, it'll be the return of the combination between me and Misaki-kun, eh?

21:30.980 --> 21:35.100
And Wakabayashi-kun's in Grunwald.

21:35.750 --> 21:36.950
Misaki-kun,

21:36.950 --> 21:38.300
Hyuga-kun,

21:38.300 --> 21:39.710
Matsuyama-kun,

21:39.710 --> 21:41.100
Misugi-kun,

21:41.100 --> 21:42.630
Ishizaki...

21:42.630 --> 21:44.290
I'm coming!

21:44.290 --> 21:45.100
And,

21:45.100 --> 21:49.620
together with all of you, I'll be playing on the world stage in France.

21:51.140 --> 21:54.420
I'll be fighting against rivals from around the world!

22:03.180 --> 22:09.020
Preview

22:03.920 --> 22:05.880
The Japanese Junior Youth team,

22:05.880 --> 22:09.060
is about to have a scrimmage against Grunwald, the team Wakabayashi-kun plays for.

22:09.060 --> 22:11.750
Since I got clean bill of health from the doctor, I'm here in Germany.

22:11.750 --> 22:17.350
Team Japan is at wits end against Karl Heinz Schneider,

22:17.350 --> 22:19.630
the Young Emperor with a cool head and a burning heart.

22:19.630 --> 22:22.610
Will the first hurdle we face be our last?

22:22.610 --> 22:24.420
Next time, on Captain Tsubasa:

22:23.540 --> 22:33.090
Humiliating Test Match

22:24.420 --> 22:26.170
Humiliating Test Match.

22:26.170 --> 22:27.180
Look forward to it!

22:27.180 --> 22:30.070
Work towards tomorrow. Score!

